Package: singletGpu
Type: Package
Title: GPU-Native Single-Cell Analysis via singlet-gpu
Version: 0.1.0
Date: 2026-04-13
Authors@R: c(
    person("Zachary", "DeBruine", email = "debruinz@gvsu.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: R interface to the singlet-gpu header-only C++20/CUDA library.
    Reads singlify .1pz count matrices zero-copy into CuSPARSE-compatible
    device CSC, then runs GPU-native log-normalization, highly-variable-gene
    selection, PCA (factornet SVD backends), NMF (factornet MU/CD/Cholesky),
    spatial deconvolution (FlashDeconv), spatial domain detection (STAGATE),
    cell fate modeling (Cell2fate neural ODE), perturbation prediction
    (PerturbGraph), generative modeling (discrete diffusion), advanced
    enrichment (ssGSEA, PROGENy), doublet detection (OmniDoublet, Scrublet),
    and consensus GEP discovery (CSI-GEP), entirely on-device.
    Results are returned as SingleCellExperiment objects with Matrix::dgCMatrix
    assays (host copy; R has no native GPU sparse type).
    Rapids-singlecell / reticulate bridge is provided as an opt-in fallback for
    Harmony batch correction and UMAP.
